<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/037G">Example <span data-tag="037G">5.3.4.24</span> <span class="named">(Homotopy Quotients)</span>.</a> Let $G$ be a group and let $BG$ denote the associated groupoid (consisting of a single object with automorphism group $G$). Let $X$ be a simplicial set equipped with an action of $G$, which we identify with a functor $\mathscr {F}: BG \rightarrow \operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}$. Applying Corollary <a data-tag="037E" href="/tag/037E">5.3.4.22</a>, we obtain an isomorphism of simplicial sets $X_{\mathrm{h}G} \xrightarrow {\sim } \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\mathscr {F}}(BG)$, where $X_{\mathrm{h}G}$ is the homotopy quotient of $X$ by the action of $G$ (Example <a data-tag="0368" href="/tag/0368">5.3.2.15</a>). If $X$ is a Kan complex, then Corollary <a data-tag="037F" href="/tag/037F">5.3.4.23</a> guarantees that $X_{\mathrm{h}G}$ is also a Kan complex. </p>
</article>
